{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46253-the-weird-and-unexplained-thread","id":46253,"title":"The Weird and Unexplained Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T07:55:09-08:00","id":46253,"title":"The Weird and Unexplained Thread","content":"Fitting for a forum run by Gothic Horror publishers, I thought it would be fun to start a thread where we share the strange and unexplained things our world has to offer. Your area's folklore, personal stories and strange finds are all welcome. I'll start:<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/52-hertz_whale\" target=\"_blank\">The 52-Hertz Whale</a></b><br /> <br /> There is no other whale in the world like the 52-Hertz Whale. It is so named because it sings its songs at a frequency much higher than what other whales might sing \u2014 52 hertz, a wee bit higher than the lowest note on a tuba. It has never been seen, but thanks to its voice being tracked, we know <a href=\"http://www.whoi.edu/cms/images/oceanus/2005/5/v44n1-briefs12en_10079.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">what migration patterns it has</a>. It has been dubbed &quot;the loneliest whale in the world&quot;, for no other whale shares its sound, and no other whale will respond to the cries it makes while swimming in the deepest blue.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Bloop was found to be <a href=\"http://www.wired.co.uk/news/archive/2012-11/29/bloop-mystery-not-solved-sort-of\" target=\"_blank\">caused by an Antarctic icequake</a>. Booooooooo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d